add('Source/schema/policies/inference were initially frozen at 850acaf. The unscored first candidate domain exhausted at A/L0/H3 (91/96). A recorded sampling-only amendment froze eight fresh seeds per family at 5e419f0 without changing quotas, unit weights, OPEN data or any model hash. Partial admissions were archived and all sealed rows regenerated. There was no sealed evidence or policy evaluation before amendment. The sealed performance evaluation occurred once under the final freeze; two local read-only checks and the fresh-clone check reproduce its whole certificate. The clone imported only 26 hash-bound ancestor payloads and independently rebuilt OPEN fitting, sealed payloads and evidence. No G6 cache/raw payload was imported.');add()
add('## Plain-language answers');add()
answers=[
('Does Sentinel represent every supported currently legal action?', 'Yes for every action offered by the audited adapter, with exact type/actor/target/parameter parity in A/B. No offered environment actions were excluded. This relies on offered metadata; hidden eligibility is not independently reconstructed.'),
('What is known about continuation legality?', 'Only reference preconditions and conditional contract constraints. Every actual future continuation remains UNKNOWN because future survival, terminal status, target eligibility and entity state are unavailable.'),
('Do certified effects compose correctly?', 'The independently tested fields compose correctly, including declared costs, displacement, protection and material emptying. Unknown collection/delivery and service remain unknown. Dependency rewiring existence composes; exact substitute resolution is unavailable and independently shown nonidentifiable.'),
('Are unknowns retained safely, and how sensitive are decisions?', 'Yes. The frozen fallback comparison above reports decision flips and paired label sensitivity separately for A/B. It is not a deployable regret bound; that bound is NOT_IDENTIFIABLE.'),
('Does full-contract planning improve on the balanced root scorer?', 'See guarded common-root FULL_D2−balanced paired gains above. The registered material rule must pass in both families to call an improvement replicated. Expanded-root gains also include changed root coverage and training; they cannot prove that depth alone helped.'),
('Is planning sufficient, and with what OOD limits?', 'DEPLOYABLE_PLANNING_SUFFICIENT='+val(C['DEPLOYABLE_PLANNING_SUFFICIENT'])+'. The corrected positive tests are limited to the full offered root domain and known compositions. ACTION_SURFACE_SUFFICIENT=false because target/dependency semantics and exhaustive conditional coverage remain unresolved. Structural OOD was not tested.'),
('How much gap comes from coverage, scoring/private values and dynamics?', 'The paired tables measure the full/common surfaces, privileged continuation restriction, private NO_ENV residual and matched environment intervention. These overlapping diagnostics cannot allocate the total gap causally or additively. A residual is not automatically an environment problem.'),
('Which contract components matter, and what remains unidentifiable?', 'The frozen no-refit ablation table measures component sensitivity, with overlapping effects. Exact collected quantity, future eligibility and specific dependency substitute are unavailable. Reference costs are exact conditionally, but decision sufficiency is not established.'),
('Is retreat unusually difficult or dominant?', 'Compare RETREAT/NON_RETREAT raw and normalized regret above. A guarded retreat-optimum stratum measures a specific decision domain, not a retreat specialist requirement. No dominant-residual claim follows from difficulty alone; earlier G5 classification remains preserved.'),
('Are any legacy failures relevant regressions?', 'No new audited regression was found. The seven unchanged unrelated lab assertions remain PRE_EXISTING_NON_BLOCKING; platform/overlay and 15 new distinction tests pass. They were disclosed and left intact.'),
('Is counterfactual prediction justified, and for what information?', 'No readiness gate passes. First qualify observable target eligibility and the collapsed dependency relationship contract. Unknown action outcomes and target internals must be separated from exogenous dynamics; capped alternatives/private values prevent forecasting attribution.'),
('Why no world model or Oracle redesign?', 'The stage supplies neither necessity for learning nor Oracle temporal/placement evidence. It permits only an offline audit with linear heads and R0 authority. WORLD_MODEL_WORK_NOW_JUSTIFIED remains false.'),
('What exact substage next?', C['NEXT_RECOMMENDED_ACTION']+'. Its qualification should expose or explicitly mark target flags/health, preserve relation subtype needed for BYPASS, prove observable derivations, and resolve conditional search coverage before reconsidering counterfactual readiness. It has not begun.')]
answers[3]=(answers[3][0], 'Yes. Switching to the fixed root fallback changes 3.52% of A decisions and 4.08% of B decisions. Paired hit effects are +0.48pp/−0.52pp, without replicated material benefit. Unknown regret bounds remain NOT_IDENTIFIABLE.')
answers[4]=(answers[4][0], 'No replicated material improvement. On common roots, D2 gains only 0.50pp in A (95% CI −0.02 to 0.95) and 0.20pp in B (−0.39 to 0.74). Retreat gains 3.00pp/2.31pp are significant but below the 5pp materiality threshold. Expanded-root and inherited-head differences also mix feature/fitting changes; they cannot prove depth alone helped.')
answers[5]=(answers[5][0], 'No under the registered positive tests. In B/ALL, normalized-regret excess over the matched fitted comparator has corrected lower bound 0.010252, above the 0.01 margin. Most other required comparisons are NOT_TESTABLE from interval precision despite adequate row counts; they are not equivalence. Target/dependency semantics and capped conditional search independently block action-surface sufficiency. Structural OOD was not tested.')
answers[6]=(answers[6][0], 'Overall raw-known hit advantages are 1.95pp/2.91pp; LOW advantages 5.07pp/5.27pp replicate materially. Matched environment gains overall are only 1.09pp/0.81pp (95% CIs 0.64–1.57 and 0.36–1.30); LOW gains 2.74pp/2.21pp also miss materiality. Current menu coverage is exact, but future surfaces, private values, fitting capacity and budgets still differ. These overlapping diagnostics do not allocate the residual causally.')
answers[7]=(answers[7][0], 'Conditional spatial descriptors matter to this frozen policy: removing them lowers hit by 7.81pp/7.34pp, a replicated material sensitivity. No other registered descriptor ablation replicates material benefit. Target-relationship removal itself was NOT_TESTED; its root count remained intact. Exact collected quantity, future eligibility and specific BYPASS substitute remain unavailable. These are overlapping no-refit sensitivities, not additive causal shares.')
answers[8]=(answers[8][0], 'Retreat is not the dominant residual: its optimum-defined stratum contributes 19.37% of guarded raw regret in A and 15.06% in B. Its per-row raw regret is higher than non-retreat in A (14.23 versus 10.00) but similar in B (10.71 versus 10.67); its normalized regret is lower in B. There is no consistent retreat penalty across both families. The older G5 classification remains unchanged on its original domain.')
for i,(q,v) in enumerate(answers,1):add(str(i)+'. **'+q+'** '+v);add()
